  "description": "Zero-allocation, hardware-accelerated storage engine primitives engineered for modern Log-Structured Merge-Tree (LSM-Tree) architectures, embedded key-value stores, and high-throughput transactional databases.\n\nProvides the foundational low-level building blocks for the Kdouja LSM-Tree Engine:\n• Write-Ahead Logging (WAL): Monotonically increasing atomic sequence ordering, forward-only buffered streaming, and hardware-accelerated Castagnoli CRC32-C with frame masking.\n• Immutable Sorted String Tables (SSTables): Kirsch-Mitzenmacher double-hashing Bloom Filters (XxHash64), RocksDB/LevelDB-compatible prefix-shortened bytewise key comparators, and stack-allocated binary span formatters.\n• MVCC Snapshot Isolation: Lock-free snapshot visibility pinning and compaction garbage-collection pruning guards.\n• Compact Variable-Length Encoding: Zero-allocation LEB128 VarInts and ZigZag signed 32/64-bit integer codecs with canonical overlong validation.\n• High-Throughput Storage Security: Key-cached AEAD ciphers (AES-256-GCM & ChaCha20-Poly1305), HKDF key derivation, and GCRA virtual-time compaction rate limiting.",
